Patch summary:
Venus: import YV12 AHardwareBuffers on hosts that need plane layouts in
memory order.

YV12 (DRM_FORMAT_YVU420) is imported as the external format
VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM with its Cb plane as plane 1 and its Cr
plane as plane 2, so plane 1 lies after plane 2 in memory. Intel's host
drivers (hasvk, anv) require VkImageDrmFormatModifierExplicitCreateInfoEXT
plane layouts in memory order and fail vkCreateImage with
VK_ERROR_INVALID_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_PLANE_LAYOUT_EXT, so every YV12 frame
SurfaceFlinger imported failed on mb11/mb13 and RenderEngine aborted
("Failed to create a valid texture"); RADV accepts either order. YV12 is
what Ika's V4L2 decoder writes in MMAP mode and what software decoders
write. Bind the planes in memory order (Cr as plane 1) and swap the chroma
channels back in the Y'CbCr conversion Venus creates for that external
format, whose components the app does not choose (the spec ignores them
for external formats). Tested on mb11 (Broadwell, hasvk): H.264 in Chrome
plays with correct colors and no SurfaceFlinger restart.

--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_android.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_android.c
@@ -155,6 +155,20 @@
    result = vk_android_get_ahb_layout(ahb, &mod_info, layouts, VN_MAX_PLANES);
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       return result;
+   /* YV12 (DRM_FORMAT_YVU420) is the external format
+    * VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM, whose Cb plane (plane 1) lies
+    * after its Cr plane (plane 2) in memory. Host drivers that require
+    * explicit plane layouts in memory order (anv, hasvk) reject that, so
+    * bind the planes in memory order; vn_CreateSamplerYcbcrConversion
+    * swaps the chroma channels back for this external format.
+    */
+   if (create_info->format == VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM &&
+       mod_info.drmFormatModifierPlaneCount == 3 &&
+       layouts[2].offset < layouts[1].offset) {
+      const VkSubresourceLayout cb = layouts[1];
+      layouts[1] = layouts[2];
+      layouts[2] = cb;
+   }
    __vk_append_struct(create_info, &mod_info);
 
    VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo external_info = {
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_image.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_image.c
@@ -927,6 +927,13 @@
       local_info.components.g = VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_IDENTITY;
       local_info.components.b = VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_IDENTITY;
       local_info.components.a = VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_IDENTITY;
+      /* YV12 images bind their Cr plane as plane 1 and their Cb plane as
+       * plane 2 (see vn_android_ahb_image_init): swap them back.
+       */
+      if (local_info.format == VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM) {
+         local_info.components.r = VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_B;
+         local_info.components.b = VK_COMPONENT_SWIZZLE_R;
+      }
       pCreateInfo = &local_info;
 
       assert(pCreateInfo->format != VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED);
